/-!
# Two open pieces glued along a causally convex overlap: the causal relation and Cauchy surfaces

No label is marked (SCOPE). Cited, unmarked: `prop:ppcm_Cauchy` — `ETT.tex:1994`, whose proof
asserts « it is a singular flat spacetime » (`ETT.tex:2324`) without arguing the global
hyperbolicity of the gluing; Sbierski 1309.7591, **Thm 2.7** (`mghdthm:CommonExtension`,
`Maximal_GHD2.tex:411`), step 4 of its proof (p. 21, `Maximal_GHD2.tex:767–769`).

Moved from `Causal.CBG.Ppcm` by T-abs-two-piece-hoist: the section `TwoPiece` and its witness
`timelikeLine_twoPiece`, byte for byte, with the same full names and the same statements, so that
a layer-1 module may use them (`Causal.CBG.Ppcm` reaches `Causal.SingularFlat` through
`Causal.CBG.NoCorresponding` → `Causal.CBG.Pgcd` → `Causal.CBG.Geometry`). This module imports
`Causal.CurveComponents` only, which is ETT-layer (no model, transitively) and brings
`IsCauchySurfaceOn` (`Causal.Cauchy`), `AbsolutelyMinimalOn` (`Causal.Generated`) and
`timelikeLine` (`Causal.Lines`). `Causal.CBG.Ppcm` imports this module and keeps the rest of the
gluing.

> (M̃, g̃) is globally hyperbolic with Cauchy surface ι̃(M̄) […] If we denote with J ∋ t₀ the
> maximal connected subinterval of I such that γ(J) ⊆ (π ∘ j)(M), then γ|_J can be considered as
> an inextendible timelike curve in M and thus has to intersect ι(M̄). Hence, γ intersects ι̃(M̄)
> at least once. Let us now assume that γ intersected ι̃(M̄) more than once. […] But this leads to
> an inextendible timelike curve in U that does not intersect ι(M̄), a contradiction, since U is
> globally hyperbolic. (Sbierski, proof of Thm 2.7, step 4)

## What is proved (no `sorry` in this file)

* `TwoPiece D A B`: the causality `D` of `P` is absolutely minimal on `⊤`, the open pieces `A`,
  `B` cover `P`, the overlap is causally convex in each piece for that piece's relation, and the
  two relations agree between points of the overlap; `twoPieceRel` (one step in a piece, or a step
  in each through the overlap).
* `TwoPiece.symm`, `rel_trans`, `le_top_iff` (`≤_P` is `twoPieceRel`), `le_of_le_top`,
  `mem_of_le_top` (each piece is causally convex in `P`: the exit/re-entry argument),
  `exists_mid`, `diamond_top_eq`, `isCausal` (`P` is causal when both pieces are),
  `isCauchySurface` (a common Cauchy surface of the pieces, acausal in `A`, is a Cauchy surface of
  `P`, for `P` causal and Hausdorff).
* The witness (kb/0011) `timelikeLine_twoPiece`: the timelike line covered by `]-∞, 1[` and
  `]0, +∞[` is a `TwoPiece` with a proper overlap and a pair related across it.

## Hypothesis checklist

| Sbierski, step 4 | here |
|---|---|
| `M̃` covered by `(π ∘ j)(M)` and `(π ∘ j')(M')`, open | ✓ `cover`, `A B : Opens P` |
| the causal curves of `M̃` are those of the pieces, chained (Lorentzian metric glued from `g`, `g'`) | ✓ `absolutelyMinimalOn`: `≤_P` is generated by `≤_A`, `≤_B` |
| `ψ` an isometry on `U` | ✓ `agree` (the two relations coincide on the overlap) |
| `U` globally hyperbolic, used for the uniqueness of the intersection | ⚠ replaced by `convex_left`, `convex_right` (the overlap causally convex in each piece) and the acausality of `S` in `A` (`hac`) |
| `ι̃(M̄)` a Cauchy surface of `M` and of `M'` | ✓ `hSA`, `hSB`, `hSsub` |
| `M̃` Hausdorff (proved earlier in the proof) | ✓ `[T2Space P]` |
| `M̃` causal: not assumed by Sbierski | ⚠ `isCauchySurface` carries `hcaus`; `isCausal` derives it from causal pieces |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* No label is marked: the statements are the model-free core of the gluing, not an ETT statement;
  `Causal.CBG.Ppcm` applies them to the gluing of two developments along their MCGHD
  (`ppcm_twoPiece`, `ppcm_globallyHyperbolic`, `ppcm_isCauchySurface`).
* Moved, nothing else: the statements, proofs and docstrings are those of `Causal.CBG.Ppcm` before
